---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About InstaGrav"
  description="Learn about InstaGrav, your comprehensive resource for understanding gravity, instant gravity, and gravitational phenomena. Discover our mission to make complex physics accessible to everyone."
  keywords="about instagrav, gravity education, physics learning, gravitational science"
>
  <div class="about-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>About InstaGrav</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Making Gravity Accessible to Everyone</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="content-block">
        <h2>Our Mission</h2>
        <p>
          InstaGrav exists to demystify one of the universe's most fundamental forces. We believe that
          understanding gravity shouldn't require an advanced physics degree. Whether you're a curious
          student, an educator, or simply someone fascinated by how the universe works, we're here to
          help you explore gravitational phenomena in an accessible, engaging way.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="content-block">
        <h2>What is Instant Gravity?</h2>
        <p>
          The concept of "instant gravity" bridges classical and modern physics. In Newtonian physics,
          gravitational effects were thought to be instantaneous across any distance. Einstein's theory
          of relativity revealed that gravitational changes propagate at the speed of light through
          spacetime as gravitational waves.
        </p>
        <p>
          This fascinating intersection of classical and modern physics raises profound questions about
          the nature of reality, causality, and the structure of spacetime itself. At InstaGrav, we
          explore these concepts and their implications for our understanding of the universe.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="content-block">
        <h2>What We Cover</h2>
        <ul class="topics-list">
          <li>Fundamental principles of gravity and gravitational force</li>
          <li>Classical vs. relativistic interpretations of gravity</li>
          <li>Gravitational waves and their detection</li>
          <li>Time dilation and spacetime curvature</li>
          <li>Black holes and extreme gravity</li>
          <li>Practical applications of gravitational physics</li>
          <li>Latest discoveries in gravitational research</li>
          <li>Mathematical foundations made accessible</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="content-block">
        <h2>Why Gravity Matters</h2>
        <p>
          Gravity shapes everything in our universe, from the motion of planets to the evolution of
          galaxies. It determines the trajectory of spacecraft, influences the passage of time, and
          even affects GPS satellites orbiting Earth. Understanding gravity isn't just about abstract
          physics—it has practical implications for technology, space exploration, and our daily lives.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="cta-section">
        <h2>Start Exploring</h2>
        <p>Ready to dive into the fascinating world of gravity?</p>
        <a href="/blog" class="cta-button">Read Our Blog</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-hero {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a2e 0%, #16213e 100%);
    padding: 5rem 2rem 4rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .container {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .about-hero h1 {
    font-size: 3.5rem;
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #4facfe 0%, #00f2fe 100%);
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    background-clip: text;
  }

  .subtitle {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: #b0b0b0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .content-section {
    padding: 4rem 2rem;
  }

  .content-block {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .content-block h2 {
    color: #00f2fe;
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
    font-size: 2rem;
  }

  .content-block p {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: #b0b0b0;
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
  }

  .topics-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }

  .topics-list li {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: #b0b0b0;
    padding-left: 2rem;
    position: relative;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .topics-list li::before {
    content: '→';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: #4facfe;
    font-weight: bold;
  }

  .cta-section {
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 4rem;
    padding: 3rem;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a2e 0%, #16213e 100%);
    border-radius: 12px;
  }

  .cta-section h2 {
    color: #00f2fe;
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
  }

  .cta-section p {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: #b0b0b0;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem 0;
  }

  .cta-button {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.875rem 2rem;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #4facfe 0%, #00f2fe 100%);
    color: #0f0f1e;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: all 0.3s ease;
  }

  .cta-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(79, 172, 254, 0.4);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .about-hero {
      padding: 3rem 1rem 2rem;
    }

    .about-hero h1 {
      font-size: 2.5rem;
    }

    .subtitle {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
    }

    .content-section {
      padding: 3rem 1rem;
    }

    .content-block h2 {
      font-size: 1.75rem;
    }

    .content-block p,
    .topics-list li {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
